answer.worked:
The remaining lower edge is $2x-3$, so the full rectangle width is $(2x-3)+x=3x-3$.
$$\begin{align*}
P &= (3x-3)+x+(2x-3)+\frac14(2\pi x)\\
P &= 6x-6+\frac{\pi x}{2}
\end{align*}$$

Subtract the quadrant from the rectangle of width $3x-3$ and height $x$.
$$\begin{align*}
A &= x(3x-3)-\frac14\pi x^2\\
A &= 3x^2-3x-\frac{\pi x^2}{4}
\end{align*}$$

